<title>GERMANY: EMI - No any single country was policy model for ECB.</title>
<headline>EMI - No any single country was policy model for ECB.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>President of the European Monetary Institute (EMI), Alexandre Lamfalussy, said on Friday that the EMI had not taken over a policy model from any one country for the European Central Bank.</p>
<p>Lamfalussy said that the ECB model was different from that of the Bundesbank in several respects. The ECB will conduct monetary policy once monetary union is launched.</p>
<p>Lamfalussy was speaking at a press conference to present a report on the operational framework of the ECB.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
